# Corpus unit robust-clip/C02 — gap (unmet-mandatory-CQ path: measurement + variance)
#
# Source: robust-clip C02 annotation (comparative, controlled_comparison;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: FARE-CLIP preserves the original CLIP embedding structure
# better than TeCoA at matched training radius — mean clean embedding loss FARE2 32.7 vs
# TeCoA2 236.9 and FARE4 47.6 vs TeCoA4 292.7; mean adversarial loss (eps 4/255) FARE2 103.9
# vs TeCoA2 301.9 and FARE4 81.9 vs TeCoA4 335.0 (Table 14, E06).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Bundled four-cell comparison (clean/adversarial x radius {2/255, 4/255}). Binding conjunct
#     is the clean embedding loss at matched radius 2 (FARE2 vs TeCoA2); the other cells stay in
#     nl and the premise leaf refs (nearest-competitor / binding-conjunct convention).
#   * Two mandatory corpus-v1 CQs are unmet, so the controlled_comparison argument is declared as
#     a located hole with both questions opened (lowering re-done for issue #15 under
#     lara-core@0.3; until lara-core@0.2 the open mandatory obligation rejected the unit, so the
#     arg was omitted):   - measurement_validity: annotation CQ "is the single 100-step APGD
#     strong enough that     L_adv is not differentially underestimated (gradient masking)?" is
#     mandatory unmet-gap     (one APGD run, no restarts / alternative attacks / strength sanity
#     check).   - variance_reported: no leaf exists. The annotation reports only means over 500
#     images     with no variance or statistical test ("significantly lower" is means-only), and
#     corpus-v1 makes variance mandatory family-wide. The hole is not an AF node, so the claim
#     stays gap on empty complete support.
#   * baseline_parity IS met (annotation CQ1 same 500 images / same L_clean-L_adv formulas /
#     same 100-step APGD, and CQ2 matched training radius) and is discharged on the hole. The
#     optional scope CQ (does ImageNet-val distortion support the general "preserves structure"
#     wording?) is unmet-gap, so scope_match is opened (optional, no status effect).
#   * The strict table-inequality re-check adapter (annotation strict_certifier) does not exist
#     yet; the comparison lowers through the defeasible controlled_comparison.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact robust-clip at sha256:6fa440686d0a
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar ---------------

claim c02
  nl      = "FARE-CLIP preserves the original CLIP embedding structure better than TeCoA at matched training radius: mean clean embedding loss FARE2 32.7 vs TeCoA2 236.9 and FARE4 47.6 vs TeCoA4 292.7; mean adversarial loss at eps 4/255 FARE2 103.9 vs TeCoA2 301.9 and FARE4 81.9 vs TeCoA4 335.0"
  formal  = better(fare, tecoa, embedding_preservation, imagenet_val)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: Table 14's radius-matched embedding-loss cells, folded into refs per cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e06, compares(fare, tecoa, embedding_preservation, imagenet_val, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C02, evidence/tables/table14_embedding_loss.md, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N05]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(fare, tecoa, e06)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E06-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E06-Procedure]

# --- ... but only an incomplete argument (a located hole) is declarable -------------------------

# The incomplete argument: measurement_validity (one 100-step APGD run risks differential
# underestimation via gradient masking) and variance_reported (means only) have no honest leaf
# and are both mandatory, so both stay open and a1 is a hole.
arg a1 : supports(c02) by controlled_comparison(fare, tecoa, embedding_preservation, imagenet_val, e06)
  discharge baseline_parity      with e2
  open      measurement_validity
  open      variance_reported
  open      scope_match

status c02

